  {
   "id": "volatility",
   "title": "Bumpiness: volatility",
   "minutes": 2,
   "body": [
    "Two strategies can end at the same place and feel completely different on the way. **Volatility** measures how bumpy the ride is: how far daily returns spread around their average, scaled to a year.",
    "The S&P 500 has run at about 15 to 19% a year. A strategy with 30% volatility will often move twice as much as the stock market in a day, in both directions.",
    "Bumpiness also drags on growth. In the picture both paths average 10% a year, but the one with 30% volatility compounds at about 5.6% a year and the calm one at about 10.3%. Bumpy strategies are also the ones people give up on at the worst moment."
   ],
